WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.534
-Today is Friday
and that's usually

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.367
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.634
You know, I check my inbox,
I return some emails,

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.167
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:10.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
And I was running a bit behind.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.601
You guys are the best.

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.434
I'd like to write out
some thank-you notes right now.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.601
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:16.934
-[ Playing tender tune ]

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:19.601
-Wow. Fantastic.

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.033
-Happy Friday.
-Mm.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:24.701
♪♪

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:26.601
Thank you, Father's Day,

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:29.367
for being the one day each year
you get to say "I love you"

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.167
to your dad's nostrils
over FaceTime.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:34.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.167
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:42.901
Thank you,
new Jack &amp; Coke in a can,

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:44.067
for telling your guests,

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.934
"This barbecue is not going
to end well."

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.734
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.834
You drank all of them?
-Yeah.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:54.033
[Indistinct] over here.
-You drank all? Oh, man.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.801
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:59.667
Thank you, New York Times
crossword puzzles,

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.634
for making me feel
like a genius on Monday

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:03.367
and a total moron by Sunday.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:06.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:08.834
"I don't know.
I don't know words."
-Yeah. "What?"

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.200
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.567
-Thank you,
roadside fireworks tents,

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.033
because nothing is
more reassuring

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:18.567
than an explosives store
designed

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.634
to pack up and leave town
as fast as possible.

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:22.000
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.167
"Let's go!
-"Get in the car!"

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.567
[ Whistling ]

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:26.601
[ Southern accent ]
It done blowed up."

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:29.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.067
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.901
Thank you,
clicking Skip Credits,

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:36.734
for being what I do because I
don't have 45 seconds to spare

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:39.367
while I watch three hour-long
episodes of TV.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.400
"I don't have time for that."

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.534
-"A waste of my time."
-Yeah, waste of my time.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:48.767
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:51.067
Thank you, centipedes,

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:52.901
for being the Rockettes of bugs.

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:55.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:02.934
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:06.167
Thank you, drawing the sun
in the corner...

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:07.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:09.834
-What?
What?!

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:15.200
-...helping me hide my deepest,
darkest secret --

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:17.634
I don't know what the other

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:19.501
three-quarters of the sun
look like.

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:22.434
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:27.701
-Unless you do a drawing.

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.300
-That was my actual drawing
-That was your drawing

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.467
you drew today?
-from this morning, yeah.

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.000
[ Laughter ]
-And you sent a thank-you note

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.100
to your own drawing?

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:35.734
-Was it to my own drawing?

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:38.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:39.834
♪♪
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.801
Thank you, ripped jeans,

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:44.000
for letting my knees
get the window seat.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.400
[ Laughter and applause ]
Yeah, that's what I'm
talking about.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.067
Those are our "Thank You Notes."
We'll be right back

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:49.133
[ Cheering ]
with Tracee Ellis Ross.

